What is your proudest success as a software engineer?

While working in my previous role, I identified the existing loop hole (buggy logic) which was costing the money. Actually, for all the files invoked by the batch job, it stores the data in the Aurora Database but while working in one of the project, I identified that the table has the millions of the rows and was not used by any other applications. So, I proposed to my tech lead that, we need data in that table to exist for only 7 days and after that we can delete the data, which will save us from the storage and query runtime cost. So, we implemented Time To Live (TTL) in that table and saved our teams from the bucks. Because of this work, I was also awarded with Verisk Way to Go award which I am most proud of till date. 


